    {
      "topic": "Finite Tate pairing and exact scalar count",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The coefficient pairing Tr_k/F_l([t^(m-1)]xy) is perfect even when the residue degree is divisible by l. Its Tate dual is A_m(epsilon alpha^-1). Local duality and the Euler characteristic give the exact exponent m(d+1)+min(m,c_alpha); no residue-degree division or finite-cocycle lifting occurs. m=0 and the resonant negative control are treated correctly."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Exact torsion subgroup and diagonal count",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The source muG is the preimage of l-primary torsion in topological abelianization, not a pro-l Sylow subgroup. Local reciprocity and the deep-unit logarithm give torsion-free rank d+1; additive maps vanishing on muG are counted by q^(m(d+1)). The stated source inertia and finite torsion projection conditions are preserved."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Original primal module and prescribed basis",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The count uses source W1, E_A plus epsilon odd blocks, not the paired dual. The explicit w1=(1-P)w conjugation has the correct coboundary sign, preserves the square-zero primal module and gives the same continuous diagonal characters. Typed columns have exactly a and b entries; full rank is n+2nu and upper rank n+nu, including an empty odd family or block."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Successive width filtration",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "After smaller widths vanish, the (i,j) conjugation coefficient is exactly psi_i psi_j^-1. Each quotient injects into scalar cocycles; no lifting or splitting is assumed. Multiplicities are one for equal types and r for unequal types. The resulting C_v=sum w_ij c_ij is finite by the actual nonresonance condition."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Arithmetic source interface and quantifiers",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The original local group is unrestricted by global transpose polarization. At split ordinary places the Euler and local-abelianization degrees agree and sum to [L+:Q]. Glob.Hom preserves each fixed local map, so fixed point, characters, odd family and witnesses give one C_v for every truncation and every auxiliary level. The exact leading-term cancellation matches W1BoundArithmeticRankTwo."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Scope",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Only the ordinary local supplier is supplied. The normalized arithmetic point, global duality, distinguished-place estimates, patched-module arguments and other global suppliers remain separate. No whole RH or GRH node closes."
    },
